WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.126 --> 00:00:05.126
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:06.785 --> 00:00:09.508
I mean, the strength coming out from you.

3
00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:12.279
I'm serious, I'm not just stroking you.

4
00:00:12.279 --> 00:00:14.885
It's, you've got something pretty magical here.

5
00:00:14.885 --> 00:00:15.940
You don't know how much that means to me,

6
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.730
because I, you have lived that life.

7
00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.490
Well, we have lived parallel lives,

8
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.600
Yeah.
In many ways,

9
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.657
Yeah.
So hearing that...

10
00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.830
Well, you have something magical here.

11
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.413
The feeling is amazing. So you're gonna,

12
00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:29.794
you're gonna take over television.

13
00:00:29.794 --> 00:00:33.149
(audience cheering)

14
00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:38.143
You have no idea how much your your approval means to me.

15
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.013
Oh, thank you.

16
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.403
I mean, let's talk about, you know, 1979,

17
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.200
what was that decade like for you?

18
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.640
Because there was some really crazy things that happened.

19
00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:00.640
'79 to '89 from a professional point of view

20
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.640
were the dark years because I had lost my career.

21
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.510
From a personal point of view,

22
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.890
I couldn't have been happier because I got married in '78.

23
00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.270
I finally found the love of my life.

24
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.920
I could spend the rest of the show,

25
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.760
just talking about how she saved me.

26
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.260
I dated her secretly for three and a half years

27
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.379
because I didn't want Tiger Beat to find out.

28
00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:22.310
(Donny laughing)

29
00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.300
and then once the news got out that I got married

30
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.099
and maybe some of you did this, I won't hold it against you.

31
00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:31.350
(Drew chuckling)

32
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:36.019
But fans literally had Donny Osman record burning parties

33
00:01:36.019 --> 00:01:36.978
(audience gasping)

34
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:41.610
and sent the most scathing letters to Debbie.

35
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.240
And she's this sweet little girl from Billings, Montana.

36
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.130
She is the most amazing woman and saved my life really

37
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.910
because I was going through some really dark times.

38
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.900
It took me about 10 years

39
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.100
before things started kicking back in again,

40
00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.040
'cause that's when Soldier Of Love hit in '89.

41
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.230
But I had tried Broadway in a show

42
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.480
called Little Johnny Jones.

43
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.740
And we opened and closed the same night,

44
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.830
that hurts.
(Donny laughing)

45
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.223
And I couldn't get a record deal.

46
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.660
I couldn't even get arrested.

47
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.520
I mean, it was, I couldn't do anything.

48
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.160
It was, everything was gone.

49
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.100
You getting married, the fans abandon.

50
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.620
Yeah.
When you got married,

51
00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:28.170
how did you know to lean into your wife,

52
00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.290
instead of saying, you're the root cause of this?

53
00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.370
How did you know to lean in with family

54
00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.770
and see the reality of what was happening

55
00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.860
rather than turn it on them?

56
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.693
Okay.

57
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.050
Because of what state I was in

58
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.773
prior to getting married to her.

59
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.180
There was a concert that I did in Hawaii

60
00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.280
and the place was packed,

61
00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.890
thousands and thousands of people screaming.

62
00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.470
And I went back to our condo.

63
00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:58.990
We had a condo there at the time

64
00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.610
and I found a little corner in the room in that condo.

65
00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.510
And I rolled myself up into a ball

66
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.180
and started crying my eyes out, uncontrollably.

67
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.390
And my brother, Jay, walks in and he sees me.

68
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.810
He said, "Donnie, what's wrong?"

69
00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.913
And I said, "Jay, I'm lonely.

70
00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:17.780
I'm just lonely."

71
00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.160
He said, "Donnie,

72
00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.540
20,000 girls were just screaming your name.

73
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.410
How could you be lonely?"

74
00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.430
I said, "I don't know, but I'm lonely."

75
00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.460
I was in such a desperate place

76
00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.830
that Debbie pulled me out of it.

77
00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.830
And whenever I make a decision in my life,

78
00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.940
the first thing I think about is her,

79
00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.090
how does it affect her?

80
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.970
And then the second, how does it affect my children?

81
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.360
And the third now is how does that affect my grandchildren?

82
00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.960
Then I'm fourth.

83
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.350
If all four of those are a green light, then I'll do it.

84
00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.520
And I think that's what's really helped

85
00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.490
this 43 year marriage is that she comes first.

86
00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:01.050
But I love what I do.

87
00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.050
It's not, I mean the applause and everything,

88
00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.160
when I walked out and everybody was just applauding

89
00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:10.160
and everything, the love that ensued is just, it's euphoric.

90
00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.010
And here's the problem.

91
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.250
If I depended on that all the time,

92
00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.237
then my downs would be really down.

93
00:04:19.237 --> 00:04:20.070
Yup.

94
00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:24.070
So what I do, and people make fun of me for it

95
00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.830
because I go home, I'll mow my grass.

96
00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.400
I'll take my garbage out.

97
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.597
I'll do the domestic things that,

98
00:04:29.597 --> 00:04:32.590
you know, I could have somebody do all that for me.

99
00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:36.930
But I do that because it's down to balancing.

100
00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:39.200
I look at my friend,

101
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.850
Michael Jackson and I had a great relationship.

102
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.970
We would laugh.

103
00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.210
We'd call each other on the phone

104
00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.770
and we'd laugh about the similarities of our families

105
00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.870
and the difference, the last time I spoke with him,

106
00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.680
he said, "I just need some normalcy in my life."

107
00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.270
I said, "Come to my home, let your kids swim with my kids.

108
00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.780
No one will know you're there."

109
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.710
He said, "I think I need to do that."

110
00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:01.543
And he never took me up on it.

111
00:05:01.543 --> 00:05:03.200
That's the last time I spoke with him.

112
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.260
So looking at that and all the other celebrities

113
00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.680
and peers and whatever,

114
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.000
colleagues that have influenced my life

115
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.040
and I've been around,

116
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.710
I see so many people have lost it

117
00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.835
because they don't know how to balance.

118
00:05:15.835 --> 00:05:16.668
Yep.

119
00:05:16.668 --> 00:05:17.880
I love the adulation.

120
00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.310
I love the standing ovations at the end of a show.

121
00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.680
I love that. I eat it up.

122
00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.848
And it's a drug and I need it,

123
00:05:24.848 --> 00:05:26.680
(Donny laughing)

124
00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.880
but I also need to go home and be a father,

125
00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:30.630
and a husband and a grandpa.

126
00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.477
You know, sometimes we can feel sorry for ourselves.

127
00:05:32.477 --> 00:05:35.290
"I've been dealt such a bad hand of cards.

128
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.090
Why God, why?"

129
00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:38.538
Well, do something about it.

130
00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:39.810
Play those cards.

131
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.150
Play those cards, you know, do something with your life.

132
00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.550
Don't constantly feel sorry for yourself,

133
00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.750
I mean, and I have,

134
00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.790
I've sat back and I'm guilty of it too.

135
00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:50.190
Say, why, why, why?

136
00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.467
And then you just say,

137
00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:56.720
"Give me the strength to just play these cards

138
00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.650
and make something of my life."

139
00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.340
I so agree with that.
(audience clapping)

140
00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.500
All right, you had Donnie and Marie.

141
00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:06.333
I mean, first of all,

142
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:07.330
let's just talk about the first show.

143
00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:08.163
Who?
That's why,

144
00:06:08.163 --> 00:06:09.780
Johnny and Marie.
Oh, Marie, oh yeah, Marie.

145
00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:10.820
Marie, that's right.
I mean,

146
00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.810
that show was just so major for everybody.

147
00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.030
We had so much fun.

148
00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:17.230
I mean, what was that like?

149
00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.880
We had no idea how much work we were getting into.

150
00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.760
And because we were doing like,

151
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.840
as far as music is concerned, an album a week,

152
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.440
let alone the comedy and the performances.

153
00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.260
And it was just overwhelming,

154
00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.070
but we were young and we had the stamina,

155
00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:36.890
Yeah.
but it was huge.

156
00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.470
It was great for the time.

157
00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:39.850
I've embraced it.

158
00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:42.000
The memories of working with my sister.

159
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.070
Yes, there were times that were difficult,

160
00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.940
but I loved working with her.

161
00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.930
It's, the only word I can call it is magic.

162
00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.670
There's a magic between the two of us

163
00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.650
that when we're both on stage together,

164
00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:55.000
something clicks.

165
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.080
Okay, so not only do you have a new album,

166
00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.070
but you have a new Vegas show.

167
00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.723
And I was wondering what you could tell us about

168
00:07:01.723 --> 00:07:02.556
both those things.
Well, you know,

169
00:07:02.556 --> 00:07:03.389
a lot of people will say,

170
00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:05.290
"Well, is it going to be like the Donnie and Marie show?

171
00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.180
No,

172
00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:08.740
I did not want to try to recreate something

173
00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.440
that she's not going to be a part of.

174
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:12.273
Right.

175
00:07:12.273 --> 00:07:15.170
So this show was so fun to put together

176
00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:17.210
because it's, talk about this is your life.

177
00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.690
I've tried to fit six decades of show business

178
00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.640
into a 90-minute show, and I did it.

179
00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.401
I just released my 65th album. And I thought,

180
00:07:25.401 --> 00:07:26.610
(audience cheering)

181
00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:30.040
so, I thought, so, so,

182
00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.813
Do you mean this one?

183
00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:33.993
Yeah, there it is.

184
00:07:33.993 --> 00:07:37.810
So it's titled "Start Again."

185
00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.370
But I thought, okay, which album

186
00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.830
and which music do I put into this show?

187
00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.880
So I said, I'm going to put every song

188
00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.623
I've ever recorded into the show.

189
00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.680
There is a segment,

190
00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.040
and it's my favorite segment of the show,

191
00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.000
where the audience takes over.

192
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.920
All 65 albums are on the huge screens behind me.

193
00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.830
They can pick any album, any song from any album.

194
00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.650
And we go three, four, and we do it.

195
00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:02.430
Well, I cannot wait to see this Opus.

196
00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.540
I am gonna be there in Vegas.

197
00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.373
Oh, please let me know when you're there.

198
00:08:04.373 --> 00:08:05.630
Oh, are you kidding me?

199
00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.608
Oh, please let me know.

200
00:08:06.608 --> 00:08:08.460
Oh, I'm there.

201
00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.293
I am there.
(audience clapping)

202
00:08:09.293 --> 00:08:13.060
I cannot thank you enough for this life-changing,

203
00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.860
meaningful conversation.

204
00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.558
Go to our website, obviously,

205
00:08:16.558 --> 00:08:19.550 line:15%
for all the information on everything you heard today

206
00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:22.810 line:15%
about the show and the album and everything.

207
00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.380 line:15%
Oh, also everybody in the audience

208
00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.853 line:15%
is going home with this album.

209
00:08:25.853 --> 00:08:30.853
Oh, fantastic.
(audience cheering)

210
00:08:32.563 --> 00:08:35.395
(Donny chuckling)
Thank you,

211
00:08:35.395 --> 00:08:37.967
thank you, thank you.

212
00:08:37.967 --> 00:08:40.550
(upbeat music)

